================================================================================
SPEC LESSON
================================================================================

The spec's recommended launch method (`.../MacOS/OpenScanner 2>&1 | tee ...`, run from a
terminal) would have masked #72 entirely: a terminal launch's cwd is the build tree, where
`FindUiDir()`'s relative candidates resolve and the page loads normally. #72 only surfaces
under an `open`-style launch (Finder/Spotlight/double-click), which is how a real user
actually launches a `.app`. The spec should require at least one `open`-style launch
alongside the terminal-redirect one, specifically to catch this class of cwd-dependent bug
that a terminal launch cannot reproduce.
